---
// "One currency, three fidelities": tier cards + the Straight-talk callout.
---

<section id="tiers" class="cql-tiers">
  <div class="cql-container cql-section">
    <h2 class="cql-h2">One currency, three fidelities</h2>
    <p class="cql-lead">
      costQL prices in <strong>work-ms</strong>: the summed real work a query causes. The
      tiers aren't different products; they're how sharply your API's instrumentation lets
      the same engine see.
    </p>

    <div class="cql-tiers__grid">
      <div class="cql-tier">
        <span class="cql-tier__tab">T1</span>
        <h3 class="cql-tier__heading">Any API. Today.</h3>
        <div class="cql-tier__body">
          Black-box wall-clock. Works against any GraphQL endpoint you can send queries to,
          with zero server changes. This is where every API starts, at ~4% measured error.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cql-tier">
        <span class="cql-tier__tab">T2</span>
        <h3 class="cql-tier__heading">Per-resolver work</h3>
        <div class="cql-tier__body">
          Your server emits per-resolver timings; parallel work stops hiding inside elapsed
          time. Under light sharing, T2 already matched T3 (11% vs 11%).
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cql-tier cql-tier--active">
        <span class="cql-tier__tab">T3</span>
        <h3 class="cql-tier__heading">Sharing, observed</h3>
        <div class="cql-tier__body">
          Loader keys and cache status: dedup counted exactly, batch curves learned, paid
          hosts named. Where schemas share heavily, this is the difference between 315% and
          12% error.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="cql-callout">
      <span class="cql-callout__label">Straight talk:</span>
      <span>
        the demo packs are T3 because we instrumented the demo servers. Your first pack will
        be T1. That's the designed starting point, and it already gives you a safe ceiling.
        T2/T3 need your server to emit <a href="/docs/instrumentation/">one trace extension</a>.
        <a href="/docs/tiers/">The full tier story →</a>
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
